          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2da3744-e927-4743-818f-9e48000dbb8f",
          "text": "读懂陈述",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
              "text": "等式与同余",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "44bd6cec-b311-4e6b-b960-8f1cbbe28190",
                  "text": "[陈述] Eq",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 陈述\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u_1} → α → α → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe equality relation. It has one introduction rule, `Eq.refl`.\nWe use `a = b` as notation for `Eq a b`.\nA fundamental property of equality is that it is an equivalence relation.\n```\nvariable (α : Type) (a b c d : α)\nvariable (hab : a = b) (hcb : c = b) (hcd : c = d)\n\nexample : a = d :=\n  Eq.trans (Eq.trans hab (Eq.symm hcb)) hcd\n```\nEquality is much more than an equivalence relation, however. It has the important property that every assertion\nrespects the equivalence, in the sense that we can substitute equal expressions without changing the truth value.\nThat is, given `h1 : a = b` and `h2 : p a`, we can construct a proof for `p b` using substitution: `Eq.subst h1 h2`.\nExample:\n```\nexample (α : Type) (a b : α) (p : α → Prop)\n        (h1 : a = b) (h2 : p a) : p b :=\n  Eq.subst h1 h2\n\nexample (α : Type) (a b : α) (p : α → Prop)\n    (h1 : a = b) (h2 : p a) : p b :=\n  h1 ▸ h2\n```\nThe triangle in the second presentation is a macro built on top of `Eq.subst` and `Eq.symm`, and you can enter it by typing `\\t`.\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "陈述",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f8fbff",
                    "color": "#1e3a8a",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#93c5fd"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "453a4c62-0449-41fd-893a-356a71b14a90",
                  "text": "[证明] Eq.mpr",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α β : Sort u} → α = β → β → α\n```\n\n**文档**\nIf `h : α = β` is a proof of type equality, then `h.mpr : β → α` is the induced\n\"cast\" operation in the reverse direction, mapping elements of `β` to elements of `α`.\n\nYou can prove theorems about the resulting element by induction on `h`, since\n`rfl.mpr` is definitionally the identity function.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "707f5acd-87dd-438f-b467-91653eb197ac",
                  "text": "[证明] Eq.rec",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** recursor\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u_1} → {a : α} → {motive : (a_1 : α) → a = a_1 → Sort u} → motive a ⋯ → {a_1 : α} → (t : a = a_1) → motive a_1 t\n```\n\n**文档**\n（无 docstring）",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "recursor"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "7aa659da-aed6-4e0f-9d29-7fd2e9217f8f",
                  "text": "[证明] Eq.symm",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Sort u} {a b : α}, a = b → b = a\n```\n\n**文档**\nEquality is symmetric: if `a = b` then `b = a`.\n\nBecause this is in the `Eq` namespace, if you have a variable `h : a = b`,\n`h.symm` can be used as shorthand for `Eq.symm h` as a proof of `b = a`.\n\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cd60764f-c899-47db-b3c0-883afa046362",
                  "text": "[证明] congrArg",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** theorem\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Sort u} {β : Sort v} {a₁ a₂ : α} (f : α → β), a₁ = a₂ → f a₁ = f a₂\n```\n\n**文档**\nCongruence in the function argument: if `a₁ = a₂` then `f a₁ = f a₂` for\nany (nondependent) function `f`. This is more powerful than it might look at first, because\nyou can also use a lambda expression for `f` to prove that\n`<something containing a₁> = <something containing a₂>`. This function is used\ninternally by tactics like `congr` and `simp` to apply equalities inside\nsubterms.\n\nFor more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality)",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "theorem"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "9ba72097-ab85-450b-883e-7ccc8c86e340",
                  "text": "[证明] rfl",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "ad555784-8f13-4708-9adc-106138bf4c6b",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Sort u} {a : α}, a = a\n```\n\n**文档**\n`rfl : a = a` is the unique constructor of the equality type. This is the\nsame as `Eq.refl` except that it takes `a` implicitly instead of explicitly.\n\nThis is a more powerful theorem than it may appear at first, because although\nthe statement of the theorem is `a = a`, Lean will allow anything that is\ndefinitionally equal to that type. So, for instance, `2 + 2 = 4` is proven in\nLean by `rfl`, because both sides are the same up to definitional equality.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "c2da3744-e927-4743-818f-9e48000dbb8f",
              "data": {
                "note": "**概念** 等式与同余（Eq / congr）\n\n**锚点** 6 个\n\n**概念依赖（聚焦内）**\n（聚焦子图内无跨概念依赖）",
                "tags": [
                  "concept",
                  "equality"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#eff6ff",
                "color": "#1e40af",
                "fontWeight": "bold",
