            {
              "id": "07f12366-b94d-4d26-bee5-13e14b8e2c52",
              "text": "商类型",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "1b3b9a2e-29e0-4c62-a689-afa9dfbef8ad",
                  "text": "[证明] Quot",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "07f12366-b94d-4d26-bee5-13e14b8e2c52",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** quotient\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → (α → α → Prop) → Sort u\n```\n\n**文档**\nLow-level quotient types. Quotient types coarsen the propositional equality for a type `α`, so that\nterms related by some relation `r` are considered equal in `Quot r`.\n\nSet-theoretically, `Quot r` can be seen as the set of equivalence classes of `α` modulo `r`.\nFunctions from `Quot r` must prove that they respect `r`: to define a function `f : Quot r → β`,\nit is necessary to provide `f' : α → β` and prove that for all `x : α` and `y : α`,\n`r x y → f' x = f' y`.\n\n`Quot` is a built-in primitive:\n * `Quot.mk` places elements of the underlying type `α` into the quotient.\n * `Quot.lift` allows the definition of functions from the quotient to some other type.\n * `Quot.sound` asserts the equality of elements related by `r`.\n * `Quot.ind` is used to write proofs about quotients by assuming that all elements are constructed\n   with `Quot.mk`.\n\nThe relation `r` is not required to be an equivalence relation; the resulting quotient type's\nequality extends `r` to an equivalence as a consequence of the rules for equality and quotients.\nWhen `r` is an equivalence relation, it can be more convenient to use the higher-level type\n`Quotient`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "quotient"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "3e651674-15e4-42f1-8249-f8d6162b1079",
                  "text": "[证明] Quot.liftOn",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "07f12366-b94d-4d26-bee5-13e14b8e2c52",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → {β : Sort v} → {r : α → α → Prop} → Quot r → (f : α → β) → (∀ (a b : α), r a b → f a = f b) → β\n```\n\n**文档**\nLifts a function from an underlying type to a function on a quotient, requiring that it respects the\nquotient's relation.\n\nGiven a relation `r : α → α → Prop` and a quotient's value `q : Quot r`, applying a `f : α → β`\nrequires a proof `c` that `f` respects `r`. In this case, `Quot.liftOn q f h : β` evaluates\nto the result of applying `f` to the underlying value in `α` from `q`.\n\n`Quot.liftOn` is a version of the built-in primitive `Quot.lift` with its parameters re-ordered.\n\n[Quotient types](lean-manual://section/quotients) are described in more detail in the Lean Language\nReference.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "4903cc5f-0a13-4647-a3a6-eff9ab280bfc",
                  "text": "[证明] Quot.mk",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "07f12366-b94d-4d26-bee5-13e14b8e2c52",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** quotient\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → (r : α → α → Prop) → α → Quot r\n```\n\n**文档**\nPlaces an element of a type into the quotient that equates terms according to the provided relation.\n\nGiven `v : α` and relation `r : α → α → Prop`, `Quot.mk r v : Quot r` is like `v`, except all\nobservations of `v`'s value must respect `r`.\n\n`Quot.mk` is a built-in primitive:\n * `Quot` is the built-in quotient type.\n * `Quot.lift` allows the definition of functions from the quotient to some other type.\n * `Quot.sound` asserts the equality of elements related by `r`.\n * `Quot.ind` is used to write proofs about quotients by assuming that all elements are constructed\n   with `Quot.mk`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "quotient"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "f72af504-2960-4782-8035-f420b77c9f5b",
                  "text": "[证明] Quot.sound",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "07f12366-b94d-4d26-bee5-13e14b8e2c52",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** axiom\n\n**模块** `Init.Core`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n∀ {α : Sort u} {r : α → α → Prop} {a b : α}, r a b → Quot.mk r a = Quot.mk r b\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe **quotient axiom**, which asserts the equality of elements related by the quotient's relation.\n\nThe relation `r` does not need to be an equivalence relation to use this axiom. When `r` is not an\nequivalence relation, the quotient is with respect to the equivalence relation generated by `r`.\n\n`Quot.sound` is part of the built-in primitive quotient type:\n * `Quot` is the built-in quotient type.\n * `Quot.mk` places elements of the underlying type `α` into the quotient.\n * `Quot.lift` allows the definition of functions from the quotient to some other type.\n * `Quot.ind` is used to write proofs about quotients by assuming that all elements are constructed\n   with `Quot.mk`; it is analogous to the [recursor](lean-manual://section/recursors) for a\n   structure.\n\n[Quotient types](lean-manual://section/quotients) are described in more detail in the Lean Language\nReference.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "axiom"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "060b3111-9060-4193-8bca-1229aee36202",
              "data": {
                "note": "**概念** 商类型（Quot）\n\n**锚点** 4 个\n\n**概念依赖（聚焦内）**\n- 等式与同余（Eq / congr）：type 2 / proof 1",
                "tags": [
                  "concept",
                  "quot"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#f0fdf4",
                "color": "#166534",
                "fontWeight": "bold",
                "shape": "round",
                "borderColor": "#34d399"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "f94bd6f2-5a0e-48dd-aba6-d2ac04b3dc7c",
              "text": "元素访问",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "e097390e-7cd3-4645-b02b-9df7f6da8686",
                  "text": "[证明] GetElem?",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "f94bd6f2-5a0e-48dd-aba6-d2ac04b3dc7c",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.GetElem`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n(coll : Type u) → (idx : Type v) → outParam (Type w) → outParam (coll → idx → Prop) → Type (max (max u v) w)\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe classes `GetElem` and `GetElem?` implement lookup notation,\nspecifically `xs[i]`, `xs[i]?`, `xs[i]!`, and `xs[i]'p`.\n\nBoth classes are indexed by types `coll`, `idx`, and `elem` which are\nthe collection, the index, and the element types.\nA single collection may support lookups with multiple index\ntypes. The relation `valid` determines when the index is guaranteed to be\nvalid; lookups of valid indices are guaranteed not to fail.\n\nFor example, an instance for arrays looks like\n`GetElem (Array α) Nat α (fun xs i => i < xs.size)`. In other words, given an\narray `xs` and a natural number `i`, `xs[i]` will return an `α` when `valid xs i`\nholds, which is true when `i` is less than the size of the array. `Array`\nadditionally supports indexing with `USize` instead of `Nat`.\nIn either case, because the bounds are checked at compile time,\nno runtime check is required.\n\nGiven `xs[i]` with `xs : coll` and `i : idx`, Lean looks for an instance of\n`GetElem coll idx elem valid` and uses this to infer the type of the return\nvalue `elem` and side condition `valid` required to ensure `xs[i]` yields\na valid value of type `elem`. The tactic `get_elem_tactic` is\ninvoked to prove validity automatically. The `xs[i]'p` notation uses the\nproof `p` to satisfy the validity condition.\nIf the proof `p` is long, it is often easier to place the\nproof in the context using `have`, because `get_elem_tactic` tries\n`assumption`.\n\n\nThe proof side-condition `valid xs i` is automatically dispatched by the\n`get_elem_tactic` tactic; this tactic can be extended by adding more clauses to\n`get_elem_tactic_extensible` using `macro_rules`.\n\n`xs[i]?` and `xs[i]!` do not impose a proof obligation; the former returns\nan `Option elem`, with `none` signalling that the value isn't present, and\nthe latter returns `elem` but panics if the value isn't there, returning\n`default : elem` based on the `Inhabited elem` instance.\nThese are provided by the `GetElem?` class, for which there is a default instance\ngenerated from a `GetElem` class as long as `valid xs i` is always decidable.\n\nImportant instances include:\n  * `arr[i] : α` where `arr : Array α` and `i : Nat` or `i : USize`: does array\n    indexing with no runtime bounds check and a proof side goal `i < arr.size`.\n  * `l[i] : α` where `l : List α` and `i : Nat`: index into a list, with proof\n    side goal `i < l.length`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "d4f0736f-47f7-4b03-bc49-bb7fdfc183be",
                  "text": "[证明] GetElem?.getElem?",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "f94bd6f2-5a0e-48dd-aba6-d2ac04b3dc7c",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.GetElem`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{coll : Type u} → {idx : Type v} → {elem : outParam (Type w)} → {valid : outParam (coll → idx → Prop)} → [self : GetElem? coll idx elem valid] → coll → idx → Option elem\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe syntax `arr[i]?` gets the `i`'th element of the collection `arr`,\nif it is present (and wraps it in `some`), and otherwise returns `none`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ab1c3fb5-9a74-468c-8318-de4a71b65ceb",
                  "text": "[证明] GetElem?.mk",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "f94bd6f2-5a0e-48dd-aba6-d2ac04b3dc7c",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** constructor\n\n**模块** `Init.GetElem`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{coll : Type u} → {idx : Type v} → {elem : outParam (Type w)} → {valid : outParam (coll → idx → Prop)} → [toGetElem : GetElem coll idx elem valid] → (coll → idx → Option elem) → ([Inhabited elem] → coll → idx → elem) → GetElem? coll idx elem valid\n```\n\n**文档**\n（无 docstring）",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "constructor"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": true,
              "parentId": "060b3111-9060-4193-8bca-1229aee36202",
              "data": {
                "note": "**概念** 元素访问（GetElem? / getElem?）\n\n**锚点** 3 个\n\n**概念依赖（聚焦内）**\n- 内部管道（equation compiler / recursor / match）：type 4 / proof 1\n- Option 与可空值：type 2 / proof 0",
                "tags": [
                  "concept",
                  "getelem"
                ]
              },
              "style": {
                "background": "#f0fdf4",
                "color": "#166534",
                "fontWeight": "bold",
                "shape": "round",
                "borderColor": "#34d399"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "e39d514e-b0ab-4774-9297-1756978d995f",
              "text": "序关系",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "f8a30690-7c78-4596-83f5-665df791dae9",
                  "text": "[证明] LT",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
