            {
              "id": "e7f9f6b8-dc36-4050-8b27-66623f0698fd",
              "text": "自然数与加法",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "0b56cdc0-b353-4eae-8785-7b921ee1ad1f",
                  "text": "[证明] Nat",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "e7f9f6b8-dc36-4050-8b27-66623f0698fd",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nType\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe natural numbers, starting at zero.\n\nThis type is special-cased by both the kernel and the compiler, and overridden with an efficient\nimplementation. Both use a fast arbitrary-precision arithmetic library (usually\n[GMP](https://gmplib.org/)); at runtime, `Nat` values that are sufficiently small are unboxed.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "4859ce69-f06c-4b85-8532-b0aadf28606f",
                  "text": "[证明] Nat.lt",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "e7f9f6b8-dc36-4050-8b27-66623f0698fd",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nℕ → ℕ → Prop\n```\n\n**文档**\nStrict inequality of natural numbers, usually accessed via the `<` operator.\n\nIt is defined as `n < m = n + 1 ≤ m`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
