                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "9a265e2e-0f0f-4788-bc74-815ec71013ad",
                  "text": "[内部] id",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "0663966c-bee4-4381-85a9-0e7f2d9b6c55",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 内部\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\n{α : Sort u} → α → α\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe identity function. `id` takes an implicit argument `α : Sort u`\n(a type in any universe), and an argument `a : α`, and returns `a`.\n\nAlthough this may look like a useless function, one application of the identity\nfunction is to explicitly put a type on an expression. If `e` has type `T`,\nand `T'` is definitionally equal to `T`, then `@id T' e` typechecks, and Lean\nknows that this expression has type `T'` rather than `T`. This can make a\ndifference for typeclass inference, since `T` and `T'` may have different\ntypeclass instances on them. `show T' from e` is sugar for an `@id T' e`\nexpression.\n\n**说明** equation compiler / recursor / match 管道，默认折叠。",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "内部",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f9fafb",
                    "color": "#6b7280",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "6a42d36d-b6ed-42be-8796-ccfd06f0f25e",
                  "text": "[内部] outParam",
                  "children": [],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "0663966c-bee4-4381-85a9-0e7f2d9b6c55",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 内部\n\n**类型** definition\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nSort u → Sort u\n```\n\n**文档**\nGadget for marking output parameters in type classes.\n\nFor example, the `Membership` class is defined as:\n```\nclass Membership (α : outParam (Type u)) (γ : Type v)\n```\nThis means that whenever a typeclass goal of the form `Membership ?α ?γ` comes\nup, Lean will wait to solve it until `?γ` is known, but then it will run\ntypeclass inference, and take the first solution it finds, for any value of `?α`,\nwhich thereby determines what `?α` should be.\n\nThis expresses that in a term like `a ∈ s`, `s` might be a `Set α` or\n`List α` or some other type with a membership operation, and in each case\nthe \"member\" type `α` is determined by looking at the container type.\n\n**说明** equation compiler / recursor / match 管道，默认折叠。",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "内部",
                      "definition"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f9fafb",
                    "color": "#6b7280",
                    "fontSize": 12,
                    "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "isExpanded": false,
              "parentId": "86a345c5-ac90-4f84-8bd2-399c1d454712",
              "data": {
